---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { owner } from '../data/owner.mjs';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | CheckVitalsNow"
  description="What information CheckVitalsNow collects, how it is used, how third-party services handle data, and the choices you have."
  h1="Privacy Policy"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what information {site.name} ({site.url.replace('https://', '')}) collects when you visit, how
    we use it, and the choices you have. {owner.name && <>The site is operated by {owner.name}.</>}
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not ask you to create an account. If you leave a comment, we store only the name and comment you type.</li>
    <li>We use Google AdSense to show ads. Google and its partners may use cookies to show ads based on your visits to this and other websites.</li>
    <li>You can turn off personalized ads at any time (see "Advertising" below).</li>
    <li>Websites we link to have their own privacy policies.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Technical data</h3>
  <p>
    Like almost every website, the servers that host and deliver {site.name} automatically process technical data when
    you visit, such as your IP address, browser type, the page you requested, and the date and time. This is needed to
    deliver pages, keep the site secure, and prevent abuse. We do not use this data to identify you.
  </p>
  <h3>Comments</h3>
  <p>
    If you post a comment on a guide, we store the first name and comment you enter, the page, and the date. Comments
    are reviewed before they appear, and approved comments are public. To limit spam, we also store a one-way coded
    (hashed) version of your IP address, which we cannot turn back into the address. We do not ask for your email.
    Please do not share personal health details you would not want to be public. To have a comment removed, contact us.
  </p>
  <p>
    The comment form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to check that you are a person and not a bot. Turnstile processes
    technical data from your browser for this check, as described in
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
  <h3>Messages you send us</h3>
  <p>
    If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you choose to write. We use it only to reply to you and
    to fix any issue you report, and we keep it only as long as needed for that.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} uses Google AdSense, an advertising service provided by Google, to show ads. Third-party vendors,
    including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website or other websites. Google's use
    of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visits to this site and/or other
    sites on the internet.
  </p>
  <p>Your choices:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising at
      <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">www.aboutads.info</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Learn more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener" target="_blank">how Google
      uses information from sites that use its services</a>.
    </li>
    <li>You can also block or delete cookies in your browser settings.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Where the law requires it, such as for visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, and Switzerland, we
    ask for your consent before personalized ads are shown. {site.name} does not use analytics cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>Other websites and services</h2>
  <p>
    Our guides link to outside sources, such as government health agencies and medical journals. When you follow a link,
    you leave {site.name}, and that website's own privacy policy applies.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some images may be loaded from third-party image services, such as Unsplash, which receive standard technical data
    such as your IP address when your browser loads the image.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To deliver and secure the website</li>
    <li>To answer messages and correct errors</li>
    <li>To review, publish, and protect comments from spam and abuse</li>
    <li>To comply with legal obligations</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your privacy rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, including several U.S. states such as California, you may have the right to know what
    personal information we hold about you, to ask us to correct or delete it, and to opt out of its sale or sharing.
    Advertising cookies set by Google and its partners may count as "sharing" for cross-context behavioral advertising
    under some state laws. You can opt out using the choices listed under "Advertising and cookies" above. To make a request, contact
    us through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. We will not treat you differently for using your rights.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} is written for adults and is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal
    information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served over an encrypted (HTTPS) connection. No method of transmission over the internet is completely
    secure, but we keep the data we handle to a minimum.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy. The "Last updated" date at the top shows when it last changed.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy? Reach us through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
